  message: "UNREVIEWED DRAFT PATCH EXISTS, produced out-of-band 2026-08-05: a workflow subagent given a READ-ONLY brief for an unrelated design review implemented this item instead (py.py Case 2g: resolve an ast.Call receiver via _resolve_call_target and look up ClassName.method like Case 2c; +21 src lines, +116 test lines). It was reverted from the working tree unexamined and saved to the session scratchpad as UNAUTHORIZED-wi-makij.patch. Treat it as a sketch, not a fix: it reached no test gate, no PR, no review, and its receiver-resolution approach and its is_instantiation interaction are unverified. If this item is picked up, start from the item, not the patch -- red tests first per the normal protocol; the patch may inform the shape."  # f8f4
- op: discuss  # 4f01
  at: '2026-08-06T04:53:49Z'  # 4f01
  by: agent  # 4f01
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4f01
  clock: 4  # 4f01
  nonce: 4f01  # 4f01
  message: "Rolled up under class item INV-linub-nokij-gibim-rovok-moros-gural-domip-rimof (filed 2026-08-06), which now holds isbefore on this item. NOT a duplicate finding: the class exists because three per-analyzer items share one invariant, and because reading _match_propagation_entry / _lookup_named_entry showed the chain has FOUR links, not one. Emission (L2) is where these items sit; receiver evidence (L3) and the io-boundary F3 gate (L4) are downstream and can refuse an edge that emission successfully adds. So a fix scoped to emission alone can move zero findings while looking like a win at the analyzer. Do not start a fix here until the class measurement fills go/rust/objc and reads the declining branch in each failing analyzer."  # 4f01
- op: discuss  # 8ed5
  at: '2026-08-17T02:07:13Z'  # 8ed5
  by: agent  # 8ed5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8ed5
  clock: 5  # 8ed5
  nonce: 8ed5  # 8ed5
  message: "TITLE LARGELY OBSOLETE. \"Chained method calls emit no call edge\" is now false for\nseven of the nine at-risk languages. Measured 2026-08-16, dev 0d305fe0e4, via\nINV-linub's chain_probe (production _match_propagation_entry, controls reported).\n\nCHAINED-site emission, all nine languages:\n\n    emit:     go, java, objc, python, rust, scala, swift\n    NO EDGE:  javascript, kotlin        <- WI-nasuf's cell, unchanged\n\nAnd python's CHAINED site does not merely emit, it MATCHES: Path(raw).write_text(x)\ncarries module_hint=pathlib.Path and reaches the catalogue entry. Constructor\nreceiver typing closed it. python is now the only language clean on all three\nchain_probe sites.\n\nWHAT REMAINS UNDER THIS TITLE is not emission. Every other CHAINED row is\n\"emit, NOMATCH\" with module_hint=external -- the edge exists and the F3 gate\ncorrectly refuses it for want of a receiver type. That is INV-linub's L3, not\nthis item's L2. An emission-shaped fix here would now move nothing.\n\nRECOMMEND folding the emission clause into INV-linub's L3 work and keeping this\nitem only if it is re-scoped to a specific remaining language. Not applied --\nflagged for the owner, since two of the languages it named (javascript, kotlin)\nare WI-nasuf's and the rest have moved."  # 8ed5
- op: discuss  # 6c07
  at: '2026-09-03T22:09:24Z'  # 6c07
  by: agent  # 6c07
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6c07
  clock: 6  # 6c07
  nonce: 6c07  # 6c07
  message: "RE-RAN THIS ITEM'S OWN REPRO ON dev 7f6c0493b0, 2026-09-03:\n    plain = Fernet(key).decrypt(token)   -> instantiates Fernet only; NO calls edge for .decrypt\n    Path(\"/tmp/out\").write_bytes(plain)  -> python:pathlib.Path:0-0:write_bytes:unresolved (typed, catalogue-reachable)\nSo the SINK half of the filed shape is fixed (PR #254, constructor-root typing)\nand the SOURCE half is not: `Fernet` is not an I/O-catalogue constructor, so\n`_receiver_type` returns None and the unknown-type Call root emits NOTHING --\nwhich is INV-luhug's shape exactly. The assigned form `f = Fernet(key);\nf.decrypt(token)` emits `python:external:0-0:decrypt:unresolved` (an edge, no\ntype), so the four built-in plaintext sources and four sanitizers are still\nunreachable in BOTH forms. NOT closing on this. The fix for both is the next\nPR: (1) INV-luhug -- an unknown-type non-Name root emits the same `external`\nplaceholder the assigned form does (PR #254's pinned asymmetry flips; its\nrecorded re-evaluation trigger is \"a consumer that distinguishes no-edge from\nuntyped-edge\", and INV-busis's escape classification is that consumer); (2) an\nIMPORTED PascalCase constructor types its instance as `<module>.<Class>` in\nboth forms, the way WI-jubag already reads PascalCase as construction, so\n`cryptography.fernet.Fernet.decrypt` matches. Sized 2026-09-03 (pure AST):\nreceiver sites typed by an imported PascalCase ctor -- mitmproxy 2,225, poetry\n2,901, pretix 3,597 (most are project classes already typed for the assigned\nform; the library share is the new reach)."  # 6c07
