  nonce: b676  # b676
  message: "DONE IN PR #752 (dev d0080868c6), on this item's OWN repro, re-run on the merged tree:\n    plain = Fernet(key).decrypt(token)   -> python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:decrypt:unresolved (call_construct method)\n    Path(\"/tmp/out\").write_bytes(plain)  -> python:pathlib.Path:0-0:write_bytes:unresolved\nand the decrypt edge reaches `cryptography.fernet.Fernet.decrypt` through\nproduction `_match_propagation_entry` over the SOURCE index (pinned by\n`test_the_instance_reaches_the_taint_catalogue`). Both halves of the filed\ntwo-line shape now emit AND match: the sink half by PR #254 (constructor-root\ntyping), the source half by this PR (an imported PascalCase constructor types\nits instance; an unknown-type non-Name root emits the placeholder). The four\nbuilt-in plaintext sources and four sanitizers are reachable in both the\ninline and the assigned form for the first time.\nThe 2026-08-17 note's re-scope stands as the item's final shape: the \"chained\nmethod calls emit no call edge\" clause was refuted for seven of nine languages\nbefore this PR; the two that still emit nothing (javascript, kotlin) are\nWI-nasuf's, next in the owner's queue, and the remaining \"emit, NOMATCH\"\nrows are INV-linub L3 per language."  # b676
